  <prompt>SCOPE CHANGE (2026-07-08, owner decision, post-Phase-D): this task no longer builds a "KPI Assessment" wizard. It builds a "Report Card" wizard targeting sprk_reportcard — the parent review artifact that sprk_kpiassessment line-items belong to. Build CreateReportCardWizard (wrapping CreateRecordWizard) + reportCardService, following the canonical workAssignmentService.ts. Steps: Associate To → Enter Info → Next Steps (NO Add Files — owner decision). Associate via applyResolverFields (Matter + Project — schema-enforced, sprk_reportcard has no other entity-specific lookups). Also add ONE additive schema column (sprk_todo → sprk_reportcard lookup, owner-approved Path A) so the Add To Do follow-on works.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE shared-UI developer + ADR-024 expert. Copy the canonical service pattern from workAssignmentService.ts. Also follow the dataverse-create-schema skill for the one schema addition.</role>
  <goal>"+" on a Report-Card-bound visual (or a KPI-Assessment-bound visual, per the registry fallback) creates a valid sprk_reportcard regarding the host Matter/Project via applyResolverFields, with assigned-resource fields collected at creation; NO files step, NO prefill; the Add To Do follow-on works end-to-end (new sprk_todo→sprk_reportcard lookup + catalog entry).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Read `projects/visual-host-create-button-r1/notes/field-manifests/reportcard.md` FIRST — it is the authoritative, owner-approved field manifest and schema-gap analysis for this task, written today specifically for this scope change. It supersedes `kpi.md` (kept for reference only — do not build against it).

      Key facts already confirmed (do not re-derive):
      - `sprk_reportcard` is FULLY ADR-024 resolver-ready today — all 5 resolver fields present, `sprk_regardingmatter`/`sprk_regardingproject` entity-specific lookups present. Zero schema delta needed for the resolver itself.
      - Enter Info manifest (owner-approved): `sprk_name` (required), `sprk_narrative`, `sprk_duedate`, plus 8 assigned-resource lookups collected AT CREATION (owner decision — see reportcard.md for the exact field list and exact schema names, including the asymmetric `sprk_assignedtolawfirm1`/`sprk_assignedlawfirm2` naming — use the real schema names, do not "fix" them).
      - NO Add Files step (owner decision) — despite `sprk_reportcard` having a `sprk_containerid` column, the wizard does not populate it or offer upload.
      - `sprk_todo` has NO lookup to `sprk_reportcard` — this blocks the Add To Do follow-on card. Owner approved Path A: add one additive lookup column (same shape/process as the two Phase-0 additions: `sprk_document.sprk_event` and `sprk_kpiassessment.sprk_regardingrecordurl`, both already live in this environment — read `.claude/skills/dataverse-create-schema/SKILL.md` and follow the same Web-API + PowerShell recipe; verify the exact PascalCase `SchemaName` Dataverse assigns via a metadata query BEFORE writing code that references it, exactly like task 002 did for `sprk_Event`).
      - Registry key: already renamed from `kpi-assessment` to `report-card` in `wizardRegistry.ts` (main session, 2026-07-08) — `ENTITY_TO_WIZARD_KEY` maps BOTH `sprk_reportcard` and `sprk_kpiassessment` to `report-card`. Your job includes replacing the ONE placeholder line `'report-card': toWizardComponent(() => import('./PlaceholderWizard'))` with the real `lazy(() => import('../CreateReportCardWizard/CreateReportCardWizard'))` import.
      - `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG` (`src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/TodoRegardingUpdateBuilder.ts`) needs a new entry for `sprk_reportcard` once the schema column exists — see reportcard.md for the exact shape.
    </background>
