  <notes>
    <completed-date>2026-07-08</completed-date>
    <summary>
      Built CreateReportCardWizard (wrapping CreateRecordWizard) + reportCardService, following the
      canonical workAssignmentService.ts pattern. Added the owner-approved additive schema column
      (sprk_todo -&gt; sprk_reportcard) and wired the wizard into wizardRegistry.ts. All 6 POML steps
      completed. Quality gates (code-review + adr-check) run unconditionally per FULL rigor — both clean,
      zero violations.
    </summary>

    <step-1-schema>
      Re-verified live: sprk_todo had NO sprk_reportcard lookup (confirmed via mcp__dataverse__describe —
      matches reportcard.md's finding, not stale). Queried sprk_todo's EXISTING sprk_regarding* lookup
      attributes' SchemaNames via direct Web API metadata call (PowerShell + az CLI token,
      EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='sprk_todo')/Attributes?$select=LogicalName,SchemaName) BEFORE writing
      any code. Result: ALL 11 existing regarding lookups on sprk_todo follow the
      "sprk_Regarding{Entity}" PascalCase convention (e.g. sprk_regardingmatter -> SchemaName
      sprk_RegardingMatter, sprk_regardingworkassignment -> sprk_RegardingWorkAssignment) — this DIFFERS
      from the manifest's speculative guess ("likely sprk_ReportCard", based on the sprk_document table's
      DIFFERENT naming convention). Followed the empirically-observed sprk_todo convention, not the
      manifest's guess.

      Created the new OneToMany relationship via Web API (RelationshipDefinitions endpoint,
      OneToManyRelationshipMetadata, CascadeConfiguration.Delete=RemoveLink matching all 11 sibling
      lookups):
        - ReferencedEntity: sprk_reportcard (1)
        - ReferencingEntity: sprk_todo (N)
        - Relationship SchemaName: sprk_sprk_reportcard_sprk_todo_RegardingReportCard (matches the
          observed sprk_sprk_{parent}_sprk_todo_Regarding{Entity} relationship-naming convention)
        - Lookup SchemaName: sprk_RegardingReportCard (CONFIRMED — the exact value used everywhere
          downstream)
        - Lookup logical name (post-creation): sprk_regardingreportcard

      Published customizations for sprk_todo + sprk_reportcard. Verified via mcp__dataverse__describe on
      sprk_todo post-publish: sprk_regardingreportcard LOOKUP (GUID) (Related table: sprk_reportcard) now
      present alongside the 11 existing regarding lookups.
    </step-1-schema>

    <step-2-catalog>
      Appended (not reordered) to TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG in
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/TodoRegardingUpdateBuilder.ts:
        { entityType: 'sprk_reportcard', entitySet: 'sprk_reportcards',
          lookupAttribute: 'sprk_regardingreportcard', navPropHint: 'reportcard' }
      lookupAttribute uses the LOGICAL name (lowercase), matching the existing 11 entries' convention.
      Updated the existing TodoRegardingUpdateBuilder.test.ts (12th entry breaks 3 hardcoded
      length/order/key assertions — fixed: listsExactlyElevenTargets -&gt; listsExactlyTwelveTargets (12),
      listsTargetsInSpecOrder appends sprk_reportcard, clearsAllOtherTenLookups -&gt;
      clearsAllOtherElevenLookups, nullsAllElevenEntitySpecificLookups -&gt;
      nullsAllTwelveEntitySpecificLookups, producesFifteenNullFieldsInTotal -&gt;
      producesSixteenNullFieldsInTotal (16 = 12 lookups + 1 recordtype + 3 text/url)).
    </step-2-catalog>

    <step-3-service>
      Created reportCardService.ts (ReportCardService class, single dataService constructor param — no
      file pipeline dependencies needed since no Files step). Flow: nav-prop discovery for sprk_reportcard
      -&gt; build payload (sprk_name required/trimmed, sprk_narrative, sprk_duedate, 8 assigned-resource
      lookups using EXACT schema field names from reportcard.md including the asymmetric
      sprk_assignedtolawfirm1/sprk_assignedlawfirm2 naming, not "fixed") -&gt; applyResolverFields
      (Matter/Project only, via REPORTCARD_REGARDING_TARGETS-consistent entity-set map) -&gt;
      createRecord('sprk_reportcard') -&gt; warnings array, never throws. No BU-defaults cascade (that
      cascade exists purely to route sprk_containerid/search-index for SPE uploads — N/A here since no
      files step). sprk_reportcardnumber deliberately never set client-side (manifest: autonumber /
      server-side).
    </step-3-service>

    <step-4-wizard>
      Created CreateReportCardWizard.tsx modeled on CreateInvoiceWizard.tsx (closer/more current template
      than CreateEventWizard.tsx, since task 030 had already completed and established the exact
      Matter+Project-only + Send Email/Add To Do/Assign Work follow-on pattern this task needed).
      Added REPORTCARD_REGARDING_TARGETS (Matter+Project, sprk_regardingmatter/sprk_regardingproject
      lookup-attribute hints) to AssociateToStep/types.ts — a new list rather than reusing
      INVOICE_REGARDING_TARGETS, because Invoice's lookupAttribute values (plain sprk_matter/sprk_project,
      no "regarding" prefix) are schema-inaccurate for Report Card's actual sprk_regardingmatter/
      sprk_regardingproject columns.

      Created CreateReportCardStep.tsx (Enter Info): Name (required) + Narrative + Due Date + 8 resource
      LookupFields, sectioned "Details"/"Assigned Resources" layout modeled on
      WizardFollowOns/steps/AssignWorkFollowOnStep.tsx's pattern for consistency.

      NO Add Files step: rather than fork CreateRecordWizard (design.md §6.3 precedent explicitly rejects
      forking as the default), added a new optional `hideFilesStep?: boolean` field to
      ICreateRecordWizardConfig (CreateRecordWizard/types.ts) and threaded it through
      CreateRecordWizard.tsx's step-array construction (filesSteps = hideFilesStep ? [] : [addFilesStep]).
      Purely additive/backward-compatible — every other wizard leaves it undefined and is byte-identical
      to before. New CreateRecordWizard.hideFilesStep.test.tsx verifies both branches at the DOM level
      (mirrors the existing lockAssociation.test.tsx pattern).

      Next Steps via WizardFollowOns: Send Email / Add To Do / Assign Work (config.followOnCards
      override), mirroring CreateInvoiceWizard's task-030 pattern exactly. IMPORTANT judgment call: the
      Assign Work follow-on does NOT attempt to link the created sprk_workassignment back to the Report
      Card, because sprk_workassignment has NO entity-specific sprk_regarding{X} lookup targeting
      sprk_reportcard (confirmed via live describe: only regardingmatter/regardingproject/
      regardinginvoice/regardingevent/regardingcommunication exist). Extending WorkAssignmentService's
      refMap to accept 'reportcard' would write partial resolver fields (id/name/url, maybe recordtype)
      with NO entity-specific lookup — itself an ADR-024 violation ("MUST include both"). Pivoted to
      comply (CLAUDE.md §6.5 Path C): Assign Work creates a standalone work assignment (still collecting
      all resource fields) with no regarding link to the Report Card. Documented inline in
      CreateReportCardWizard.tsx's file-level comment. WorkAssignmentService.ts / its formTypes.ts were
      NOT touched.
    </step-4-wizard>

